<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n97444" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στωϊκ-ός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στοά</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of a colonnade</i> or
				<i>porch</i>: hence, <u>Stoic</u> (because Zeno taught
			in the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στοὰ Ποικίλη</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, οἱ τῆς Σ. αἱρέσεως ἡγεμόνες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					<u>Comp.</u>
					2
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				13.1.57
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				14.6.3
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ Σ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				2.227S.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				6.14
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ Σ</span>. the
			<u>Stoics</u>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				2.296S.
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				3.1359
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				7.5
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ Σ. φιλόσοφοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Act.Ap.</u>
					17.18
				</span></i>
			. (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Στοϊκός</span></b>  in <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.496
			</span></i>(<span class="entity">Athenaeus</span>).)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
